      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a983204a1528d415c5ced46|full_name}: This method needs to be run but we'll look into making it more specific to avoid processing so many unused prefabs.\nThis method and much of how Udon is serialized is done specifically to work around a number of issues we encountered when dealing with Unity's Prefab and Asset systems. UdonBehaviours depend on a SerializedUdonProgram asset that contains the serialized data built from the UdonProgramSource asset. UdonBehaviours in the scene can easily be found and checked to make sure they have a valid reference to their SerializedUdonProgram asset. Prefabs on the other hand may not even exist in the scene if they are only referenced by a scene object. If a prefab loses its reference to the SerializedUdonProgram asset for its ProgramSource then it will fail to run. To avoid this prefabs are checked before the world is run or built to ensure that their references are valid. Unfortunately there is no way to know whether a prefab is \"pre-existing\" or \"made for Udon\" without checking for an UdonBehaviour.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
